<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy · Wanderply" %>

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0">
    <div class="aurora"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="relative max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-32 pb-12 sm:pt-40">
    <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-amber-300 font-semibold">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.05]">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      Wanderply is a trip planner, not a data business. We collect what the app
      needs to plan your trips, and nothing else. Last updated July 3, 2026.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-20">
  <article class="prose-invert max-w-none text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-6">

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Account data</strong> — your name, email address, and password (stored as a bcrypt hash; we never see the plain text).</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Trip content</strong> — destinations, dates, travelers, itineraries, checklists, notes, and any preferences you type in (for example dietary or accessibility notes). This is the product; it's stored so your trips exist.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Sharing data</strong> — the email addresses you invite to a trip, so we can deliver the invitation.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Documents you upload</strong> — hotel confirmations, tickets, and similar files you attach to a trip, stored privately in our cloud storage.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Quiz scores</strong> — your Travel Trivia results, kept for your personal bests.</li>
      <% if analytics_enabled? %>
        <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Usage analytics</strong> — which pages you visit and which features you use, so we can see where Wanderply is confusing or broken. Signed-in activity is tagged with your account's random ID, never your name or email. Signed-out visitors aren't given a profile at all.</li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not collect precise device location, contacts, or advertising identifiers<% unless analytics_enabled? %>, or analytics profiles<% end %>.
      The mobile apps are thin wrappers around this website and collect nothing extra.
    </p>

    <h2>How trip planning uses AI</h2>
    <p>When you ask Wanderply to build an itinerary or suggest day trips, the trip details you entered (destination, dates, pace, preferences) are sent to our AI providers — currently Anthropic and Perplexity — to generate the plan. These inputs are trip-planning text, not your account credentials. We don't send your email address or password to AI providers.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use a session cookie to keep you signed in and a CSRF token to protect forms.<%= " Our analytics provider sets a first-party cookie to recognise repeat visits from the same browser." if analytics_enabled? %>
      No advertising or cross-site tracking cookies — there are no ads.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Hosting &amp; storage</strong> — Amazon Web Services (servers, database, file storage) in the United States.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Email</strong> — Amazon SES sends invitations and account emails.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Images</strong> — trip and quiz images load from public CDNs (Pexels, Unsplash, Pixabay, Wikimedia, flagcdn, Simple Icons). Those requests carry your IP address like any image load.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Geocoding</strong> — place names on your itinerary (not your location) are looked up via Google Places or OpenStreetMap Nominatim to pin them on maps.</li>
      <% if analytics_enabled? %>
        <li><strong class="text-amber-200">Product analytics</strong> — PostHog records which pages and features are used, so we can fix what's broken. It receives your account's random ID (not your name or email), your IP address, and your browser type. It is not an ad network and we don't sell or share this with one.</li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>No selling or renting your data. Ever.</li>
      <li>No ads and no ad tracking.</li>
      <li>No reading your trips for anything other than showing them to you and the people you shared them with.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing and visibility</h2>
    <p>Your trips are private to you and the people you explicitly share them with. If you create a public share link, anyone with that link can view that trip until you revoke the link.</p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Deleted trips are soft-deleted first (so you can recover from mistakes) and then removed. To delete your account and all of its data, use the account settings or email us — we'll remove it.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Wanderply is a general-audience trip planner intended for adults planning family travel. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children under 13; accounts are meant to be created by adults.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:skchakri@gmail.com" class="text-amber-300 hover:text-amber-200">skchakri@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes materially, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
  </article>
</section>
